{"id": "EUVD-2026-82216", "enisaUuid": "a2c3c9ce-f876-32df-8a69-b20cc4294a90", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/ipoib: Drain RCU callbacks during module teardown\n\nIPoIB reclamation completions can be signaled from inside an RCU callback.\nTeardown can wake before the callback returns and unload ib_ipoib while its\ncode is still executing.\n\nClient registration failure can also remove already-added devices and queue\ncallbacks. Wait after client and workqueue teardown.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb9c23733a0c50e136bd40c27cb60023cc58e22c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a6dc313f9661f80e4ed43461d7ed5615c2450ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8917353966d1d5a486437dd0dd68a2cf8ecb136", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7bc08d7f9338c9f9c09965e5d020591c793a80cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b3330cfc097db2d31f47ad09261967630270d66", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8dc5ffcb8efcc01e44dd1ebc490eaae72de3fadf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24ce944721dcd92ae62e7a448d770e2a3e79f5fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31b7c700670830a0e8a4cdcd451c88a13cc5dc48"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93108", "GHSA-v32w-6gxx-mfwq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11694968-8364-3b74-990c-237a304fef57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "150eeb5d-c5b8-3ee3-a8bb-0e66cb661c47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "2fed1ba8-8188-3cb9-aa1e-6bd9420b1927", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b63b70d8774175b6f8393c495fe455f0fba55ce1 <d8917353966d1d5a486437dd0dd68a2cf8ecb136"}, {"id": "32c2d2c8-fbaf-3652-a7c7-1ef3b09ee6af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 